   $q$Read the sentences: "The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks. An exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure." Which revision fixes the fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks, this was an exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks; an exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-phrase"},{"text":"The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks an exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-comma-before-appositive"},{"text":"The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks, an exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The debate team practiced rebuttals for weeks, an exercise that sharpened their ability to respond under pressure.$q$, $q$"An exercise that sharpened" is a noun phrase that renames the practice, so a comma attaches it to the main clause. Adding "this was" creates a second independent clause, which turns the fragment into a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
