   $q$Read the sentences: "The Roman road network stretched across thousands of miles. It allowed soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly. Many modern highways still follow its routes." Which choice most effectively combines the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The Roman road network stretched across thousands of miles, it allowed soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly, many modern highways still follow its routes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Stretching across thousands of miles and allowing soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly, many modern highways still follow the routes of the Roman roads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier-created"},{"text":"The Roman road network, which stretched across thousands of miles and allowed soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly, and many modern highways still follow its routes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subject-without-main-verb"},{"text":"The Roman road network, which stretched across thousands of miles and allowed soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly, still guides the routes of many modern highways.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The Roman road network, which stretched across thousands of miles and allowed soldiers, merchants, and messengers to travel quickly, still guides the routes of many modern highways.$q$, $q$The correct choice gives "network" the main verb "guides" and tucks the other details into a "which" clause. In the choice ending "and many modern highways still follow its routes," the subject "network" never receives a main verb.$q$, 'draft', null)
