   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft states a clear claim near its opening?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Dragonflies are among the oldest flying insects, and they can be found on nearly every continent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Faleolo's tracking data suggest that migrating dragonflies wait for favorable winds instead of flying steadily.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Faleolo's study is about dragonflies and the way they travel along the coast during autumn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"More scientists should study dragonflies, since they are far more interesting than butterflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Faleolo's tracking data suggest that migrating dragonflies wait for favorable winds instead of flying steadily.$q$, $q$Sentences 3 through 6 show the insects resting and then flying far on north wind days, so a claim about waiting for favorable winds fits. The choice about what the study is about names a topic without making a point.$q$, 'draft', 'cb089783-aab3-5f17-8e7f-a0da3a07aa3b')
